We want to solve the equation \(x = e^{-x}\), which can be rearranged to form: \[f(x) = x - e^{-x} = 0\] Take the derivative of \(f(x)\) with respect to \(x\): \[f'(x) = 1 - \left(-e^{-x}\right) = 1 + e^{-x}\] Substitute \(f(x)\) and \(f'(x)\) into the general Newton-Raphson iterative formula: \[x_{n+1} = x_n - \dfrac{f(x_n)}{f'(x_n)}\] \[x_{n+1} = x_n - \dfrac{x_n - e^{-x_n}}{1 + e^{-x_n}}\] Find a common denominator to combine the terms: \[\begin{aligned}
x_{n+1} &amp;= \dfrac{x_n\left(1 + e^{-x_n}\right) - \left(x_n - e^{-x_n}\right)}{1 + e^{-x_n}} \\[1.5ex]
&amp;= \dfrac{x_n + x_n e^{-x_n} - x_n + e^{-x_n}}{1 + e^{-x_n}} \\[1.5ex]
&amp;= \dfrac{x_n e^{-x_n} + e^{-x_n}}{1 + e^{-x_n}} \\[1.5ex]
&amp;= \dfrac{(1 + x_n)e^{-x_n}}{1 + e^{-x_n}}
\end{aligned}\] This derived updating expression matches Option C. \[\boxed{\text{C. } x_{n+1} = \dfrac{(1+x_n)e^{-x_n}}{1+e^{-x_n}}}\] <div class="sol-block sol-keypoints"><div class="sol-block-title">Key points</div><ul><li><strong>Recurrence Simplification</strong>: When setting up Newton-Raphson iteration relations for symbolic options, always combine terms over a common denominator and look for common factors to simplify the expression.</li></ul></div>

