To determine the final contents of the Program Counter (\(\text{PC}\)) and the \(\text{HL}\) register pair, we track the assembly instructions execution line by line: <ol><li><strong>2710 LXI H, 30A0H</strong><br/>This instruction stands for <strong>Load Register Pair Immediate</strong>. It loads the 16-bit hexadecimal constant \(30\text{A0H}\) directly into the \(\text{HL}\) register pair. \[\text{HL} = 30\text{A0H}\]</li><li><strong>2713 DAD H</strong><br/>This instruction stands for <strong>Double Add Accumulator/Register-pair</strong>. It adds the 16-bit contents of the specified register pair (\(\text{HL}\)) to the \(\text{HL}\) register pair itself (\(\text{HL} = \text{HL} + \text{HL}\)). Performing hexadecimal addition: \[\begin{array}{rccccccl}
    \text{Hexadecimal:} &amp; \mathbf{3} &amp; \mathbf{0} &amp; \mathbf{A} &amp; \mathbf{0} &amp; \text{H} &amp; &amp; \\
    \text{Binary Grouping:} &amp; (0011) &amp; (0000) &amp; (1010) &amp; (0000) &amp; &amp; &amp; \\ &amp; 0011 &amp; 0000 &amp; 1010 &amp; 0000 &amp; &amp; &amp; (\text{Initial } \text{HL}) \\
    + &amp; 0011 &amp; 0000 &amp; 1010 &amp; 0000 &amp; &amp; &amp; (\text{Initial } \text{HL}) \\
    \cline{2-5}
    \text{Binary Sum:} &amp; 0110 &amp; 0001 &amp; 0100 &amp; 0000 &amp; &amp; &amp; \\
    \cline{2-5}
    \text{Hex Conversion:} &amp; \downarrow &amp; \downarrow &amp; \downarrow &amp; \downarrow &amp; &amp; &amp; \\
    \text{Result:} &amp; \mathbf{6} &amp; \mathbf{1} &amp; \mathbf{4} &amp; \mathbf{0} &amp; \text{H} &amp; &amp; 
    \end{array}\] Thus, the contents of the register pair become \(\text{HL} = 6140\text{H}\).</li><li><strong>2714 PCHL</strong><br/>This instruction copies or transfers the 16-bit contents of the \(\text{HL}\) register pair straight into the Program Counter (\(\text{PC} \leftarrow \text{HL}\)). <ul><li>The value inside \(\text{HL}\) remains unchanged by this transfer.</li><li>Therefore, both registers now share the exact same value: \[\text{PC} = 6140\text{H}, \quad \text{HL} = 6140\text{H}\]</li></ul></li></ol> This matches the values stated in option (C). \[\boxed{\text{(C) } \text{PC} = 6140\text{H}, \text{HL} = 6140\text{H}}\] <div class="sol-block sol-keypoints"><div class="sol-block-title">Key points</div><ul><li><strong>DAD rp:</strong> Executes 16-bit addition with the \(\text{HL}\) register pair as the destination target.</li><li><strong>PCHL:</strong> Performs an unconditional structural branch by overwriting the \(\text{PC}\) address tracking register with the current data held in \(\text{HL}\).</li></ul></div>

The characteristic equation is determined by setting \(1 + G(s) = 0\): \[1 + \frac{s + 8}{s^2 + \alpha s - 4} = 0 \implies s^2 + (\alpha + 1)s + 4 = 0\] RH Table: \[\begin{array}{c|cc}
s^2 &amp; 1 &amp; 4 \\
s^1 &amp; \alpha + 1 &amp; 0 \\
s^0 &amp; 4 &amp; 
